The great polymorphing discussion continues --
No, it's not from lycanthropy, otherwise my character would turn into the
type of monster that bit me.
I went into wizard mode and wished for a cursed amulet of change and a cursed 
ring of polymorphing and just carried them around for awhile.  Nothing 
happened, so I guess that's not it.
But it happened again today -- wes5 the Samurai roaming around the mines 
when *poof* he turns into a stone golem.  (not a bad critter to 'morph
into -- one time I turned into a floating eye -- all I could do was freeze
creatures and wait to turn back into a human).  Anyway there was no mention of 
stepping on a trap, and no trap or trap marker was left behind (unlike
those polymorphing traps where the gnome deliberately steps onto the trap
and turns into a Nazgul, etc.).  I dunno -- maybe it's a one-time polymorph
trap that disappears after one shot.  Opinions?

